  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An element crystallises in a face&ndash;centred cubic (fcc) unit cell with cell edge a. The distance between the centres of two nearest octahedral voids in the crystal lattice is:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>a</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In FCC octahedral voids are present at the edge centers and body center.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0039_41f12a8e3335.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 280px;\" /></p><p>Minimum distance between centers of two octahedral voids</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
